session:pr542Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #536 (split from #533) asked for Query::Ask and FILTER (NOT) EXISTS to stop materialising the full WHERE-clause solution set before checking whether any solution exists — an unselective ASK/EXISTS pattern was doing full enumeration just to answer a boolean. Investigation of sparql_parser/src/execute/{mod,components,bgp}.rs found that issue #165 had already built exactly the needed machinery: eval_components_budgeted threads an optional row budget to the last top-level WHERE-clause component, and for a BGP triple pattern with no repeated variable that budget reaches all the way into Datastore::quads_matching_limited's lazy .take(), genuinely stopping the index scan rather than just truncating a materialised Vec afterwards. So instead of building new short-circuit machinery, this PR is a thin wiring change: the three call sites that previously called the unbudgeted eval_components (the Query::Ask arm in execute_inner, and the Expression::Exists/NotExists arms in expressions.rs) now call eval_components_budgeted with Some(1). This reuses the #165 budget's documented boundary as-is: only the last top-level component is budgeted, earlier components in a multi-pattern join are still fully materialised — an honest partial short-circuit, not one reaching through every join stage, which is called out explicitly in the PR description. Semantics are unchanged: NOT EXISTS still inverts the same boolean, and EXISTS/NOT EXISTS never leaked inner bindings into the outer scope before or after (confirmed both by reading the call sites, which discard the returned solutions except for is_empty(), and by a new regression test asserting no binding leakage). Tests were added in sparql_parser/tests/ask_exists_short_circuit.rs covering ASK true/false, the vacuously-true empty WHERE clause, unselective many-match patterns (the case the short-circuit optimises), zero-match patterns, the ASK+FILTER boundary (last-component-only budgeting), a repeated-variable pattern (which disables the quad-take gate and exercises the solutions-level cap instead), FILTER EXISTS/NOT EXISTS correctness, and the binding-leakage check. A timing-based proof of the speedup was deliberately not added (fragile per the issue's own guidance); the structural proof is that the change routes through the already-tested #165 budget/quad-limit machinery unmodified." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:542 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr542 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
